  "final_answer": "If the backend endpoint `GET /api/admin/settings/*PARAM*` (where `*PARAM*` is the variable `key`) is deleted, the following TypeScript consumers in the Angular frontend will be **broken** (this is a **BREAKING** change):\n\n### 1. Direct Service Consumer\n* **`AdminService`** (`ui-ngx/src/app/core/http/admin.service.ts`)\n  * **Method:** `getAdminSettings<T>(key: string, systemByDefault?: boolean, config?: RequestConfig)`\n  * **Impact:** This method makes the actual HTTP GET call to `/api/admin/settings/${key}` and will fail.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Component/Page Consumers\nThe following components directly invoke `AdminService.getAdminSettings` to retrieve configuration settings:\n\n* **`GeneralSettingsComponent`** (`ui-ngx/src/app/modules/home/pages/admin/general-settings.component.ts`)\n  * **Calls:** \n    * `this.adminService.getAdminSettings<GeneralSettings>('general')` (to load general system settings)\n    * `this.adminService.getAdminSettings<DeviceConnectivitySettings>('connectivity')` (to load connectivity settings)\n\n* **`MailServerComponent`** (`ui-ngx/src/app/modules/home/pages/admin/mail-server.component.ts`)\n  * **Calls:**\n    * `this.adminService.getAdminSettings<MailServerSettings>('mail')` (to load outgoing SMTP mail server settings)\n\n* **`SmsProviderComponent`** (`ui-ngx/src/app/modules/home/pages/admin/sms-provider.component.ts`)\n  * **Calls:**\n    * `this.adminService.getAdminSettings<SmsProviderConfiguration>('sms', false, {ignoreErrors: true})` (to load SMS provider/gateway configurations)\n\n### Conclusion\nDeleting this endpoint will completely break the Admin Settings module of ThingsBoard (General, Connectivity, Mail Server, and SMS Provider setup pages). Therefore, this is a **BREAKING** change.",
